We're a small logistics company and a freight-tracking partner needs to push shipment updates into our account. Their account ID is 123456789012. Our contractor wrote this CDK for the role they'll use:

```ts
const partnerRole = new iam.Role(this, 'PartnerRole', {
  assumedBy: new iam.AccountPrincipal('123456789012'),
});

partnerRole.addToPolicy(new iam.PolicyStatement({
  actions: ['dynamodb:*'],
  resources: ['*'],
}));
```

The partner only ever needs to write rows to our `ShipmentEvents` table in us-east-2 (our account is 111122223333). Is this fine to hand over? We're not doing anything fancy on the monitoring side yet.

